# Install onto both iPhones

After any change under `app/ios/` (including NativeWrapper, CollabSync, ViewController, Settings.bundle) or `app/android/jni/` (shared with iOS), install to both phones. Do not ask. Do it.

```bash
./app/ios/scripts/install-both-phones.sh
```

Run from the rtabmap repo root. Script: `app/ios/scripts/install-both-phones.sh`. Phones: `app/ios/scripts/devices.txt`.

- Scheme `RTABMapApp`, team `F38B8K483F`, bundle `com.dnhacks.rtabmap`. Never change the signing team unless asked.
- If a phone is unplugged or unpaired, install to the one that is present and tell the user which phone was skipped.
- If both are missing, stop and say so. Do not pretend the install happened.
- Dry-run destinations only: `./app/ios/scripts/install-both-phones.sh --dry-run`
- Set `DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer` if `xcrun` cannot find `xctrace` / `devicectl` (CLT-only `xcode-select`).
- If a UDID in `devices.txt` is `REPLACE_ME`, fill it from the next successful `xcrun xctrace list devices` (use the `0000...` hardware UDID, not the CoreDevice UUID).

## Not Xcode

Server-only C++ under `server/` does not need Xcode. Rebuild `rtabmap-collab-server` and kickstart the LaunchAgent:

```bash
cmake --build build --target rtabmap-collab-server
launchctl kickstart -k "gui/$(id -u)/com.dnhacks.rtabmap-collab-server"
```
